{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"horrendous-limpid-chamois","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\n`overlap_drain = \"off\"` (rebar.toml:209, landed 08-28 via 2dbdcc8abe2c) disables the enrichment drain, but the PRODUCER side still runs: every plan-review certification unconditionally appends an `ENQUEUE_ENRICH` event to the tickets store (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:216-225` — best-effort `_enqueue_queue.enqueue(...)` with no config check), and `suggest_duplicate_tickets = true` (rebar.toml:40) keeps the advisory overlap feature nominally on.\n\nEvidence: 95 `ENQUEUE_ENRICH` commits appended to the tickets branch in the last 2 days with the drainer off — durable store writes into a queue nothing consumes. Each is a git commit + push on the shared store (the project's top fragility surface; see `.scratch/stability-analysis/E1-store-prototype.md` §enrich and `06-plan.md` A.0.2).\n\n## Fix shape\n\nGuard the certification-time enqueue on the same effective config that governs the drain, so producer and consumer cannot disagree; and set `suggest_duplicate_tickets = false` for this project. Historical queue events stay untouched (read-only history; no backlog drain, no deletion). Read the config through the standard config path (must pass `scripts/check_config_reads.py`).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] With `overlap_drain = \"off\"`, a plan-review certification appends NO `ENQUEUE_ENRICH` event (regression test proves it: certify against a throwaway store with drain off, assert no queue event file/commit is produced).\n- [ ] With the drain enabled, enqueue behavior is unchanged (existing tests still pass).\n- [ ] `rebar.toml` for this project sets `suggest_duplicate_tickets = false`, with the adjacent comment block (rebar.toml:38, :207) updated so the two settings no longer claim the advisory overlap stays on.\n- [ ] No existing `ENQUEUE_ENRICH`/`CLAIM_ENRICH`/`DONE_ENRICH` events are modified or deleted.\n- [ ] No new config key, env var, lock, or guard mechanism is introduced (use the existing `overlap_drain` / `suggest_duplicate_tickets` reads).\n\n## File impact\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py — guard the certification-time enqueue on the effective overlap config\n- rebar.toml — suggest_duplicate_tickets = false + comment correction\n- tests: one regression test for \"certification with drain off appends no queue event\" (extend the existing queue/attest test module rather than adding a new file)","id":"4eae-c207-7d7b-41f3","parent_id":"","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Enrich producer still appends ENQUEUE_ENRICH to the store while overlap_drain is off"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788214657591162795,"uuid":"e28d2ab9-863c-4030-8d37-12ce99afa2b5"}